  "findings": [
    {
      "classification": "reviewed",
      "detail": "source202 changes the record width from 251 to 254 float4 slots and writes the native FP32 material-frame 3x3 at record+251 on stage 0 (three slots, 48 added bytes per tetrahedron/environment). It calls femMaterialFrame(tetrahedron) for framed objects and writes identity otherwise. Runtime labels and emits these rows. This is a diagnostic capture; physical force/operator arithmetic is unchanged.",
      "id": "exact-frame-capture"
    },
    {
      "classification": "reviewed",
      "detail": "The cached-operator reader falls back to quaternion reconstruction for legacy captures without rows. If the header declares native_float32_rows_no_renormalization, absent rows fail closed. Present rows are shape-checked, checked for proper rotation, and inactive-frame rows must be identity. The source202 and source203 CPU suite logs each report 28 tests passed.",
      "id": "reader-compatibility"
    },
    {
      "classification": "follow_up",
      "detail": "The assembler payload carries exact material_frame_rows and material_frame_rows_directly_captured, but the main topology NPZ writer omits them. Its already-emitted assembled operator remains available; rebuilding that operator from topology.npz alone can fall back to quaternion reconstruction and lose the exact captured FP32 frame. This is a reproducibility gap in the diagnostic export, not a production operator defect; a separate source204 patch is warranted.",
      "id": "topology-export-gap"
    },
    {
      "classification": "reviewed",
      "detail": "source203 changes only matter/src/runtime.mm. The host allows all:all scheduling for damped fallback across Newton iterations. The kernel eligibility rule is unchanged: only a healthy exhausted primary Armijo search marks the fallback eligible; candidate RHS is rebuilt and CGLS initializes from zero. Accepted/noop/unhealthy branches remain ineligible. The original Newton certificate does not certify this direction; unchanged nonlinear Armijo and final physical certification gate acceptance.",
      "id": "all-newton-host-schedule"
    },
    {
      "classification": "limit",
      "detail": "Admission remains limited to exact damping text 1e-3, 32/64 CGLS iterations, no primary policy/right scaling/warm start, same-root true-residual certification, and existing pure-FEM/mass/capability checks. Broadening the host schedule can add up to the configured CGLS work and Armijo retries at each exhausted Newton. No performance result is established.",
      "id": "guard-cost-limit"
    }
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This is read-only source/build/CPU evidence. It does not adjudicate pending native537/538/539.",
    "No full-coupon convergence, shipping-scale, or performance claim follows.",
    "Captured material-frame rows are producer-emitted data, not an independent raw GPU-memory readback."
  ],
